The Day 211 (22:46) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as fa05d00e. The folder is gitignored, so I committed it with git add -f, as the earlier assessment commits were.

The top priority for the planner is #966: --print writes the answer twice. I reproduced it with a small local fake server and the binary built for this commit. stdout was \n{"answer": 42}\n\n{"answer": 42}, and the exit code was 0.

The same bug also breaks `--output-format json`, and #966 doesn't mention it. In that mode the streamed text lands on stdout before the JSON object, so piping it to jq fails with "Extra data".

The cause is the same for both. The streaming code in src/prompt.rs prints to stdout at four places (lines 858, 878, 1120 and 1183), and none of them checks the output mode. In print mode, main.rs only turns off colour. A fix that covers only --print would leave the JSON mode broken, so the task should fix both.

